  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN, and a string SSS of length KKK consisting of characters L\\texttt{L}L and R\\texttt{R}R only.\n\nYou have to perform KKK operations on the array. In the ithi^{th}ith operation:\n\n\nIf the array is of size 111, you do not need to perform the operation.\nElse, choose an integer XXX (1≤X&lt;∣A∣)(1\\le X \\lt |A|)(1≤X&lt;∣A∣) randomly and equi-probably and break the array AAA into subarrays A[1,X]A[1, X]A[1,X] and A[X+1,∣A∣]A[X+1, |A|]A[X+1,∣A∣], where ∣A∣|A|∣A∣ denotes the length of the array.\n\nIf Si=LS_i=\\texttt{L}Si​=L, set A:=A[1,X]A:=A[1, X]A:=A[1,X]\nIf Si=RS_i=\\texttt{R}Si​=R, set A:=A[X+1,∣A∣]A:=A[X+1, |A|]A:=A[X+1,∣A∣]\n\n\nFind the expected sum of all elements in the final array AAA after KKK operations.\n\nThe value can be represented as an irreducible fraction PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​, where PPP and QQQ are coprime integers. You need to output P⋅Q−1P \\cdot Q^{-1}P⋅Q−1 modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7), where Q−1Q^{-1}Q−1 represents the multiplicative inverse of QQQ modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7).\n\nNote that A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] denotes the subarray [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L+1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the size of the array and the number of operations respectively.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers denoting the elements of the array.\nThe third line of each test case contains a string of length KKK consisting only of characters L\\texttt{L}L and R\\texttt{R}R.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the expected sum of all elements in the final array AAA after KKK operations.\n\n\nThe value can be represented as an irreducible fraction PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​, where PPP and QQQ are coprime integers. You need to output P⋅Q−1P \\cdot Q^{-1}P⋅Q−1 modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7), where Q−1Q^{-1}Q−1 represents the multiplicative inverse of QQQ modulo (109+7)(10^9+7)(109+7).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5001 \\leq T \\leq 5001≤T≤500",
      "1≤N,K≤5001 \\leq N, K \\leq 5001≤N,K≤500",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 500500500.",
      "The sum of KKK over all test cases won't exceed 500500500.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (30 points):** The sum of NNN and the sum of KKK across all test cases won't exceed 100100100.",
      "**Subtask 2 (70 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
